# The build context is the repository root, and everything in it is sent to the
# Docker daemon and cached there - whether or not a COPY ever mentions it. The
# per-service contexts have their own files; this one is the union of both plus
# everything that only exists at the root.

# The clinical corpus and a multi-gigabyte CUDA environment. First for the same
# reason it is first in backend/.dockerignore: .gitignore does not apply here,
# and neither belongs anywhere near an image build.
backend/training/

# The weights, ~420MB, mounted read-only at runtime rather than copied in. See
# openwiki/decisions/2026-08-31-the-model-is-mounted-not-baked-into-the-image.md.
backend/models/

# Working copies of this same repository, one per agent worktree. Left in, the
# context would carry several full checkouts - including their own node_modules
# and any weights they were given.
.claude/

.git/
.github/

backend/.venv/
backend/tests/
backend/scripts/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/

frontend/node_modules/
frontend/.next/
frontend/coverage/
frontend/out/
frontend/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
npm-debug.log*

# Nothing in the image build reads these, and a stray .env holds the
# credential. backend/README.md is deliberately not excluded: pyproject.toml
# declares it as the project readme, so the dependency install fails without it.
**/.env
**/.env.*
deploy/
openwiki/
